/* mre.lps — Inform's "MRE" (Future events), by hand.
 *
 *   Food has a satisfaction period (usually 5 minutes; apple 2, pasta 125).
 *   The player is hungry.
 *   Check eating when the player is not hungry: say "You're not hungry right now."
 *   Carry out eating: now the player is replete;
 *     hunger resumes in the satisfaction period of the noun from now.
 *   At the time when hunger resumes: starvation occurs in three minutes from now;
 *     now the player is hungry.
 *   At the time when starvation occurs: if the player is hungry, end the story.
 *   Every turn when the player is hungry: say a complaint.
 *   Test me with "eat apple / z / z / z / eat candy bar / z x 9".
 *
 * Ideal transcript: a complaint at turns 4, 11, 12, 13; "You have starved" at 13.
 *
 * Two findings this spike exists for:
 *
 * 1. STORY TIME IS A FLUENT. Inform's clock advances once per turn, and an LPS
 *    turn is a burst of cycles, so "in three minutes from now" cannot be
 *    "T + 3 cycles". `turn(N)` is a fluent the command advances, and a
 *    scheduled event is a fluent naming the turn it is due.
 *
 * 2. A TURN HAS AN END. Inform runs, in order: the action, the every-turn rules,
 *    the timed events, the prompt. An every-turn rule keyed on the *command*
 *    reads the state before the action and complains on the turn the player
 *    eats. So the driver injects `end_turn` once the burst is quiescent, and the
 *    every-turn rules and the timed events key on that. Below, the script plays
 *    the driver: a command, two cycles for the burst, then `end_turn`.
 */
maxTime(60).

fluents  turn(_), hungry(_), carries(_, _), in(_, _), due(_, _), dead(_).
events   command(_), end_turn.
actions  take(_, _), eat(_, _), say(_), starve(_).

initially turn(0), hungry(player), in(player, larder),
          in(apple, larder), in(candy, larder), in(pasta, larder).

food(apple).  food(candy).  food(pasta).
satisfaction(apple, 2).  satisfaction(candy, 5).  satisfaction(pasta, 125).

%  the clock: every command is a turn
command(_) updates N to N1 in turn(N) if N1 is N + 1.

take(A, X)  initiates carries(A, X).
take(_, X)  terminates in(X, _).
eat(A, X)   terminates carries(A, X).
eat(A, _)   terminates hungry(A).
%  "hunger resumes in the satisfaction period of the noun from now"
eat(A, X)   initiates due(hunger(A), Then) if turn(Now), satisfaction(X, S), Then is Now + S.
starve(A)   initiates dead(A).

false eat(A, X), not carries(A, X).
false eat(A, X), not food(X).

%  "(first taking the apple)": the implicit take is a composite event
if   command(eat(X)) from _ to T, hungry(player) at T
then consume(player, X) from T to _.
if   command(eat(X)) from _ to T, not hungry(player) at T
then say(not_hungry) from T to _.

consume(A, X) from T1 to T2 if carries(A, X) at T1, eat(A, X) from T1 to T2.
consume(A, X) from T1 to T3 if not carries(A, X) at T1,
                              take(A, X) from T1 to T2, eat(A, X) from T2 to T3.

%  "Every turn when the player is hungry" — at the end of the turn
if   end_turn from _ to T, hungry(player) at T, turn(N) at T, not dead(player) at T
then say(complaint(N)) from T to _.

%  "At the time when hunger resumes" — a timed event, after the every-turn rules
if   end_turn from _ to T, due(hunger(A), N) at T, turn(N) at T, Then is N + 3
then terminate due(hunger(A), N) from T to T2,
     initiate hungry(A) from T to T2,
     initiate due(starvation(A), Then) from T to T2.

%  "At the time when starvation occurs: if the player is hungry, end the story"
if   end_turn from _ to T, due(starvation(A), N) at T, turn(N) at T, hungry(A) at T
then starve(A) from T to T2, terminate due(starvation(A), N) from T to T2.
if   end_turn from _ to T, due(starvation(A), N) at T, turn(N) at T, not hungry(A) at T
then terminate due(starvation(A), N) from T to _.

%  Test me with — the script plays the turn driver: command, burst, end_turn
observe command(eat(apple))  from 1 to 2.    observe end_turn from 4 to 5.
observe command(wait)        from 5 to 6.    observe end_turn from 8 to 9.
observe command(wait)        from 9 to 10.   observe end_turn from 12 to 13.
observe command(wait)        from 13 to 14.  observe end_turn from 16 to 17.
observe command(eat(candy))  from 17 to 18.  observe end_turn from 20 to 21.
observe command(wait)        from 21 to 22.  observe end_turn from 24 to 25.
observe command(wait)        from 25 to 26.  observe end_turn from 28 to 29.
observe command(wait)        from 29 to 30.  observe end_turn from 32 to 33.
observe command(wait)        from 33 to 34.  observe end_turn from 36 to 37.
observe command(wait)        from 37 to 38.  observe end_turn from 40 to 41.
observe command(wait)        from 41 to 42.  observe end_turn from 44 to 45.
observe command(wait)        from 45 to 46.  observe end_turn from 48 to 49.
observe command(wait)        from 49 to 50.  observe end_turn from 52 to 53.
observe command(wait)        from 53 to 54.  observe end_turn from 56 to 57.
